"A hypergraph reconstruction context consists of a category $\\mathfrak{C}$ of applicable prestacks, a deleting process $\\mathcal{D}:\\mathfrak{C}\\rightarrow[\\mathbb{X}^{op};\\mathbf{Cat}]$, and a natural transformation $\\gamma:\\imath_{\\mathfrak{C}}\\Rightarrow\\mathcal{D}$. For each applicable prestack $C\\in\\mathfrak{C}$ and each $V$, let $\\mathcal{D}C_V$ be the category of pieces, and call two hypergraphs **$\\mathcal{D}$-hypomorphic** when their images in $\\mathcal{D}C_V$ are isomorphic. **The deleting-process reconstruction conjecture.** For each $V$, two hypergraphs in $C_V$ are isomorphic if and only if they are $\\mathcal{D}$-hypomorphic; equivalently, each functor\n\n$$\n\\gamma_V:C_V\\rightarrow\\mathcal{D}C_V\n$$\n\nis essentially injective. This axiomatizes the ordinary and disjoint reconstruction conjectures in a common reconstruction context; the source provides no resolution."